# The two pricing modes over one sealed FRI occurrence, priced side by
# side with the Johnson row's subject: the conjectured random-words row
# (the corrected conjecture of ePrint 2025/2010 §1.5) and the proven
# threshold-halving row (ePrint 2026/858, carried with its unvetted
# status in the obligations ledger). A proven number and a conjectured
# number never blur: each witness's ledger names the assumption it
# rides on, and the analysis point arrives request-resolved, gated by
# the row's own decider into the cited window.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-family %S/../Family/Inputs/frigrind.json --emit-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json --emit-spine=%t/spine.mlir
# RUN: zkc-seal %t/spine.mlir --protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   -o %t/sealed.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/sealed.artifacts %t/sealed.mlirbc

# Conjectured: fold n/|F|, query (rho + eta_bar)^ell with the
# instance's rho = 1/512 and the requested eta_bar = 1/4096:
# (9/4096)^2 = 81/16777216. The ledger carries the conjecture entry.
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/fri-random-words-request.json -o=%t/conjectured.json %t/sealed.mlirbc
# RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=CONJ %s < %t/conjectured.json
# CONJ: "zkc.assume.random_words_conjecture"
# CONJ: "constant": "10/340282366762482138490186164457219031041"
# CONJ: "constant": "81/16777216"

# An eta_bar below the Diamond-Gruen correction floor understates the
# conjectured loss; the decider refuses it.
# RUN: not zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/fri-random-words-understated-request.json -o=%t/refused.json %t/sealed.mlirbc 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=CONJBAD %s
# CONJBAD: condition_failed at apply.conditions.S2

# Proven above the Johnson radius: fold 2^k/|F|, query (1 - delta/2)^ell
# at the requested delta = 63/64: (65/128)^2 = 4225/16384. The ledger
# carries the unvetted-status entry — the number is proven per the
# citation, and the citation's standing is a recorded obligation.
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/fri-threshold-request.json -o=%t/proven.json --headline %t/sealed.mlirbc \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=HEADLINE %s
# RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=PROVEN %s < %t/proven.json
# The display view: presentation of the exact witness — per-round
# power-of-two ceilings, the weakest round, and the ledger beside the
# number, soundcalc-comparable. The witness itself stays exact.
# HEADLINE: headline round 0: eps <= 2^-126
# HEADLINE: headline round 1: eps <= 2^-1
# HEADLINE: headline: the weakest round loses at most 2^-1 per attempt
# HEADLINE: headline obligation: zkc.assume.threshold_halving_unvetted
# PROVEN: "zkc.assume.threshold_halving_unvetted"
# PROVEN: "constant": "2/340282366762482138490186164457219031041"
# PROVEN: "constant": "4225/16384"

# A delta below the Johnson radius is outside the cited statement; the
# decider refuses to price there.
# RUN: not zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/fri-threshold-below-window-request.json -o=%t/refused2.json %t/sealed.mlirbc 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=PROVENBAD %s
# PROVENBAD: condition_failed at apply.conditions.S2
